(# The answer as it actually reads: one run-on line, never a list.

   `answer.tex` comes first, then whichever extras exist, each glued on with `\answerJoin`.
   That is a comma while the answer is running text, and nothing at all when the answer
   ended block-level -- a picture, a list -- because there is no line for a comma to sit on;
   `core/latex/utilities.tex` has the reasoning. `answer-interval` and `answer-also`
   additionally carry an i18n lead-in ("uznajte výsledky v intervale", "also accept", ...)
   and are closed with a full stop; `answer-extra` gets the join and no lead-in.

   Shared by `blocks/answer.jtex` (booklet, answer sheets, modulo sheets) and by
   `standalone.jtex` (the one-problem preview), so the preview cannot drift from the real
   thing. Needs `path_exists`, which decides against the *source* tree: the built `.tex` for
   a part that does not exist is simply never produced. An `answer.md` that exists but is
   empty needs no test of its own -- it leaves TeX in vertical mode and `\answerJoin` sees
   that.

   `\tightPictures` is what keeps a picture-only answer sitting under its problem number
   rather than a \topsep below it; the group confines it to this block. See
   `core/latex/utilities.tex`. #)
\begingroup\tightPictures%
\protectedInput{\activeDirectory/(* language.id *)/answer.tex}%
(@ set prefix = "{}/{}/{}/problems/{}".format(module.id, competition.id, volume.id, problem.id) @)%
(@ if path_exists("source/{}/{}/answer-extra.md".format(prefix, language.id)) -@)%
\answerJoin\protectedInput{\activeDirectory/(* language.id *)/answer-extra.tex}%
(@- endif -@)%
(@- if path_exists("source/{}/answer-interval.md".format(prefix)) -@)%
\answerJoin\textit{(* i18n[language.id].answers.interval *)} \protectedInput{\activeDirectory/(* language.id *)/answer-interval.tex}\!.
(@- endif -@)%
(@- if path_exists("source/{}/answer-also.md".format(prefix)) -@)%
\answerJoin\textit{(* i18n[language.id].answers.also *)} \protectedInput{\activeDirectory/(* language.id *)/answer-also.tex}\!.
(@- endif -@)
\endgroup%
